    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Arlington is the historic heart of the Town of Poughkeepsie, once bustling with shops, restaurants, banks, churches, libraries, schools, and even Vassar College.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://arlingtonhasit.org/about/history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Arlington neighborhood was known for its comfortable mix of local businesses and residential side streets, creating a pleasant pedestrian environment.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://arlingtonhasit.org/about/history/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In the 1940s and 1950s, a stock car racing facility in Arlington hosted Mutual Racing Association events, reflecting Dutchess County's post‑war auto‑racing boom.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arlington%2C_New_York",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The Arlington Revitalization Steering Committee, formed in 2000, brought together Vassar College, the Town of Poughkeepsie, Dutchess County Economic Development Corporation, and local businesses to plan long‑term revitalization.",
